          "distinct": true,
          "id": "368bcf30fe0fe775c791e490a446a40c66dbbcda",
          "message": "docs: rework root README (286→116L) + logo.svg + canonical crate-README template (sq-kuqa) (#37)\n\n* docs: rework root README — logo, badges, concise pitch, links not essays\n\nPer design sq-9jw5 / bead sq-kuqa. Replaces the 286-line front page with a\n~116-line concise README:\n\n- assets/logo.svg: currentColor wordmark (works light+dark) with the amber\n  #f5a623 spark accent — the SVG agreed in the sq-9jw5 design.\n- Logo + badge row (CI, MIT, benchmarks dashboard, MSRV, status) at the top.\n- One-paragraph pitch; three emoji sections (🚀 Quickstart / ✨ Features /\n  📚 Learn more) per the template; License last.\n- Deleted the inline Performance / Parsing / Serialisation / \"sparq vs QLever\"\n  essays — they duplicated research/ and bench/. README now LINKS the bench\n  dashboard + bench/CATALOG.md + the research verdict docs instead (obeys the\n  AGENTS.md \"no hard-coded performance numbers\" rule — none remain).\n- Per-crate Packages table folded into the ✨ Features list (every crate named)\n  + a pointer to AGENTS.md's crate map; per-crate detail lives in the per-crate\n  READMEs (sibling beads).\n- Fixed: was linking conformance-report.md (git-ignored / generated). Now links\n  the sparq-conformance crate + the committed inference report. Tracked the same\n  dangling refs in AGENTS.md/CONTRIBUTING.md as bead sq-sfvh.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add canonical concise-README template to CONTRIBUTING.md\n\nPer design sq-9jw5 / bead sq-kuqa. New \"Crate README conventions\" section is\nthe single source the per-crate README beads (sq-xogx / sq-h1s7 / sq-rt1t /\nsq-q2em / sq-puyy / sq-4kr5) follow:\n\n- Publishable crate: ~110L (cap 120), badges, exactly three emoji markers\n  🚀✨📚 + unmarked License, fixed section order (title+badges / pitch /\n  what-why / 🚀 Quickstart doctest / ✨ Features / 📚 Learn more / License).\n- Routing rule: how-tos -> SKILL.md, format/API -> rustdoc //!, design ->\n  research/, ALL perf numbers -> benchmark dashboard/harness (no baked numbers).\n- include_str!(README) + docs.rs all-features wiring; cargo test --doc gate.\n- publish=false crates: 15-line stub, no badges.\n- Tone: factual, honest about scope; relocate detail, never delete it.\n\nThe root README is the worked example of the publishable shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: make root README library example self-contained (Copilot PR #37) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jesse@jeswr.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
